  <p>
    <strong>Key Takeaway:</strong> Gravitational lensing turns massive cosmic objects into natural telescopes,
    bending and magnifying light from distant sources. This effect allows us to study the universe's earliest
    galaxies, map dark matter, and test general relativity on cosmic scales. It's one of the most powerful tools
    in modern astronomy.
  </p>
